                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M SO
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mi SO
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M SO_\ast \longrightarrow R
          %p or
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M U_\ast \longrightarrow R
          %p
            respectively. Written this way it is immediate that genera arise naturally as the value on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            (the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"}> decategorification
            ” or “de-homotopification”) of homomorphisms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            from an actual universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            to some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficient"} coefficient
            ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi SO
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M SO \longrightarrow E
          %p or
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi E
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M U \longrightarrow E
                  \\,.
          %p
            This in turn induces multiplicative morphisms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theories"} cohomology theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} represented
            by these spectra (the domain being hence
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+cohomology+theory"} cobordism cohomology theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} index
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hopkins94"}> Hopkins 94, section 3
            ).
          %p
            Such homomorphisms in turn arise naturally from
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} universal orientations in generalized E-cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⟵
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                          %mi SO
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mn 0
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mi σ
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi J
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi GL
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                          %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\ast &amp;&amp; \longleftarrow &amp;&amp; B SO
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{0}}\searrow &amp; \swArrow_\sigma  &amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{J}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; B GL_1(E)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; E Mod
                  }
          %p
            (a trivialization of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-module+bundle"} (∞,1)-module bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} associated
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spherical+fibration"} spherical fibration
            given by the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-homomorphism"} J-homomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimits"} homotopy colimits
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29Mod"} (∞,1)Mod
            this becomes an
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi SO
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⟵
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M SO \wedge E  \longleftarrow E
          %p hence a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi SO
                  %mo ⟵
                  %mi E
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M SO  \longleftarrow E
                  \\,.
          %p
            At least in some important cases, genera seem to be naturally understood as encoding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theories"} quantum field theories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            some structure, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M G
            is the classifying space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spaces"} target spaces
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-models"} sigma-models
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            itself may then be thought of as a classifying space for a certain class of QFTs, and hence the genus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo :
                  %mi M
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma : M G \to R
            can be thought of as assigning to any target space the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
          %p
            This is for instance the case at least over the point for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-hat+genus"} A-hat genus
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                    %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M Spin \to K O
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            to the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%281%2C1%29-dimensional+Euclidean+field+theories+and+K-theory"} (1,1)-supersymmetric EFT
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+particle"}> spinning particle
            ”); and for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mi String
                    %mo →
                    %mi tmf
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M String \to tmf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            to the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-dimensional+Euclidean+field+theories+and+tmf"} (2,1)-supersymmetric EFT
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string"}> heterotic string
            ”).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#Rationalization Rationalization
          %p
            When the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficient"} coefficient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            does not have additive
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion"} torsion
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi SO
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi \colon \Omega^{U/SO}_\bullet \longrightarrow R
          %p is determined already by its rationalization
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mi SO
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi \colon \Omega^{U,SO}_\bullet\otimes \mathbb{Q} \longrightarrow R \otimes \mathbb{Q}
          %p
            which is traditionally denoted by the same symbol. The rational
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+rings"} cobordism rings
            in turn are known to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+rings"} polynomial rings
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi U
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^U_\bullet\otimes \mathbb{Q} \simeq \mathbb{Q}[\mathbb{C}P^1,\mathbb{C}P^2, \cdots ]
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi SO
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℂ
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega^{SO}_\bullet\otimes \mathbb{Q} \simeq \mathbb{Q}[\mathbb{C}P^2,\mathbb{C}P^4, \cdots ]
          %p
            whose generators are identified with the cobordism classes of the manifolds which are the complex
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+spaces"} projective spaces
          %h3#LogarithmAndCharacteristicSeries Logarithm and Characteristic series
          %h4#definition_in_components Definition in components
          %p
            Given a (rational) genus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mi SU
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo →
                  %mi R
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \colon \Omega^{U,SU}_\bullet\otimes \mathbb{Q} \to R \otimes \mathbb{Q}
            one defines (we follow (
            %a{:href => "#Hopkins94"}> Hopkins 94
            ))
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                its
                %em logarithm
                to be the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series"} formal power series
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \otimes \mathbb{Q}
                given by
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi log
                        %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi P
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi z
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mo ;
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      log_\phi(z) \coloneqq \sum_{n \in \mathbb{N}} \phi(\mathbb{C}P^n) \frac{z^{n+1}}{n+1};
            %li
              %p
                its
                %em characteristic series
                (or
                = succeed ")" do
                  %em Hirzebruch series
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \otimes \mathbb{Q}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mfrac
                        %mi z
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi exp
                            %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      K_\phi(z) \coloneqq \frac{z}{\exp_\phi(z)}
                      \\,,
              %p
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi exp
                        %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp_\phi
                is the inverse of the logarithm;
            %li
              %p
                its
                %em characteristic class
                as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+characteristic+class"} universal characteristic class
                which via the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/splitting+principle"} splitting principle
                is fixed by its value on the universal line bundle as
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi R
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      K_\phi(c_1) \in H^\bullet(B U(1),R \otimes \mathbb{Q})
              %p
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1 \in H^2(B U(1), \mathbb{Z})
                denotes the universal
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ⊕
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_1 \oplus \cdots \oplus L_k
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundles"} complex line bundles
                is
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi K
                        %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\prod_{i} K_\phi(c_1(L_i))
                      \\,.
          %h4#HirzebruchSeriesViaOrientationsInGeneralizedCohomology Definition via orientations in generalized cohomology
          %p
            Suppose that the given genus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi SO
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_\bullet^{SO} \longrightarrow R
            indeed comes from an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation in generalized cohomology
            (as discussed
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#InStableHomotopyTheory"} above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi M
                  %mi SO
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\beta \;\colon\;  M SO \longrightarrow E
          %p
            for an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R\simeq \pi_\bullet(E)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            defines a
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology+theory"} complex oriented cohomology theory
          %p
            This defines (
            %a{:href => "#AndoHopkinsRezk10"}> Ando-Hopkins-Rezk 10, prop. 2.11
            ) a universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation
            of real vector bundles and hence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
            and hence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundles"} complex line bundles
            in
            = succeed "-cohomology" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi M
                  %mi SO
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi β
                  %mi E
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\beta \;\colon\; M U \longrightarrow M SO \stackrel{\beta}{\longrightarrow} E
                  \\,.
          %p
            Now rationally, i.e. for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\otimes \mathbb{Q}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi M
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi M
                  %mi SO
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi H
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi 𝕊
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\alpha \;\colon\; M U \longrightarrow M SO \longrightarrow H \mathbb{Q} \simeq \mathbb{S}\otimes \mathbb{Q} \stackrel{}{\longrightarrow} E \otimes \mathbb{Q}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Thus, given any orientation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B GL_1(E \otimes \mathbb{R})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta/\alpha
            with coefficients in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi GL
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL_1(E\otimes R)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            the difference is a class in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mi E
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℚ
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^0(X, \pi_\bullet E\otimes \mathbb{Q})^\times
          %p
            Specifically consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X= B U(1)
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+ring"} cohomology ring
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"} power series
            ring in a single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variable"} variable
            (the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1(L)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B U(1)\to B U
            both the above orientations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            pull back, so that we have a difference
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi β
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi α
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K_\beta \coloneqq \beta/\alpha \in (E_\bullet \otimes \mathbb{Q})[ [ c_1(L) ] ]
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the Hirzebruch series of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta
            (
            %a{:href => "#AndoHopkinsRezk10"}> Ando-Hopkins-Rezk 10, def. 3.10
            ).
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group+law"} formal group law
            classified via
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi MU
                    %mo •
                  %mo →
                  %mi M
                  %msub
                    %mi SO
                    %mo •
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi β
                        %mo •
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU_\bullet \to M SO_\bullet \stackrel{\beta_\bullet}{\to} E_\bullet
            then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mi z
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi exp
                        %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K_\beta(z) = \frac{z}{\exp_F(z)}
          %h3#HirzebruchFormula The Hirzebruch formula
          %p
            The central theorem of (
            %a{:href => "#Hirzebruch66"}> Hirzebruch 66
            ) expresses the genus of an arbitrary (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+class"} cobordism class
            of a) manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2n
            via the formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %munderover
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi(X)
                  \=
                  \\langle \prod_{i = 1}^n K_\phi(x_i(T X)), [X] \rangle
          %p
            in terms of the Hirzebruch characteristic series
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K_\phi
            discussed
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#LogarithmAndCharacteristicSeries"} above
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/splitting+principle"} splitting principle
          %p
            This means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi K
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{i = 1}^n K_\phi(x_i(T X))
            is the function of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+classes"} Chern classes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_k
            (i.e.
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+classes"} Pontryagin classes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi P
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_{2k}
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+classes"} Euler classes
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
            in the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i
            (the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+roots"}> Chern roots
            ”) as a polynomial in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elementary+symmetric+polynomials"} elementary symmetric polynomials
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_k(x_1,\cdots, x_n)
            and then substituting for each of these by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_k(T X)
          %p
            (see also e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "http://www.map.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/Formal_group_laws_and_genera#Construction"} ManifoldAtlas – Genera – 4.1 Construction
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#todd_genus Todd genus
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+genus"} Todd genus
            is the genus with logarithm
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mi log
                    %mi Todd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \-log_{Todd}(1-x) = \sum_{n \in \mathbb{N}} \frac{x^n}{n}
          %h3#signature_genus Signature genus
          %p
            The
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+genus"} signature genus
          %h3#AhatGenus
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A
            \-genus
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-hat+genus"} A-hat genus
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+of+a+Dirac+operator"} index of a Dirac operator
            coming from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+bundle"} spin bundle
            in KO-theory. It is given by the characteristic series
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "genus#LogarithmAndCharacteristicSeries"} characteristic series
            of the
            = succeed "-genus" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi K
                            %mover
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi e
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mfrac
                            %mi z
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mi z
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                  %mn 2
                              %mo −
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi z
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                  %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi exp
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo ≥
                                %mn 2
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi B
                                  %mi k
                              %mi k
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi z
                                  %mi k
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo !
                            %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  K_{\hat A}(e)
                  \&amp; =
                  \\frac{z}{e^{z/2} - e^{-z/2}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;=
                  \\exp\left(
                  \- \sum_{k \geq 2} \frac{B_k}{k} \frac{z^k}{k!}
                  \\right)
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_k
            is the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernoulli+number"} Bernoulli number
            (
            %a{:href => "#AndoHopkinsRezk10"}> Ando-Hopkins-Rezk 10, prop. 10.2
            ).
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-genus" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer"} integer
            on manifolds with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
          %h3#elliptic_genus Elliptic genus
          %p
            An
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            is one whose logarithm is given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi log
                    %mi ell
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mn 0
                    %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo −
                  %mn 2
                  %mi δ
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mi ϵ
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mn 4
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                  %mi d
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  log_{ell}(z) = \int_0^z (1-2 \delta t^2 + \epsilon t^4)^{-1/2} d t
          %p
            for constants
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϵ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta, \epsilon
            with non-degenerate values
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi δ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi ϵ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta^2 \neq \epsilon
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon = 0
          %p
            For degenerate choices this reproduces the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+genus"} signature genus
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-hat+genus"} A-hat genus
            above, see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+genus"} elliptic genus
            for more. For non-degenerate values one may regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            as values of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+forms"} modular forms
            of the same name and hence regard all elliptic genera together as one single genus with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi MF
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MF_\bullet(\Gamma_0(2))
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
          %h3#witten_genus Witten genus
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi SO
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  w \colon \Omega^{SO}_\bullet \longrightarrow \mathbb{Q}[ [q] ]
          %p
            is the genus with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"} power series
            ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}[ [ q ] ]
            with characteristic series given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi K
                            %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mn 2
                            %mrow
                              %mi sinh
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mn 2
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo ≥
                              %mn 1
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %msup
                                %mi q
                                %mi n
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mn 2
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %msup
                                %mi q
                                %mi n
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %msup
                                %mi q
                                %mi n
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi exp
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo ≥
                                %mn 2
                            %msub
                              %mi G
                              %mi k
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi z
                                  %mi k
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo !
                            %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  K_w(z)
                  \&amp; =
                  \\frac{z/2}{sinh(z/2)}
                  \\prod_{n \geq 1}
                  \\frac{(1-q^n)^2}{(1-q^n e^z)(1-q^n e^{-z})}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  \\exp\left(
                  \\sum_{k \geq 2} G_k \frac{z^k}{k!}
                  \\right)
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_k
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eisenstein+series"} Eisenstein series
            (
            %a{:href => "AndoHopkinsStrickland01"}> Ando-Hopkins-Strickland 01
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AndoHopkinsRezk10"} Ando-Hopkins-Rezk 10, prop. 10.9
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_k
            is proportional to the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernoulli+number"} Bernoulli number
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#AhatGenus"} A-hat genus above
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin structure
            the Witten genus takes values in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[ [ q ] ]
          %p
            On manifolds with rational
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            it takes values in (the
            = succeed "-expansion" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+forms"} modular forms
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi SL
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL_2(\mathbb{Z})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi π
                      %mi i
                      %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q = e^{2 \pi i \tau}
            then as a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            of the parameter
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
            taking values in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+half+plane"} upper half plane
            the Witten genus satisfies
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi τ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi τ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f(-1/\tau) = (-\tau)^n f(\tau)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Finally on manifolds with actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+structure"} string structure
            it takes values in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+modular+forms"} topological modular forms
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            for more.
          %h2#nonexamples Non-examples
          %h3#euler_characteristic Euler characteristic
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto \chi(X)
            is close to being a genus, but is
            %em not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
            invariant
          %p
            (this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} index
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo =
                    %mi d
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi d
                      %mo †
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = d + d^\dagger
